  "raw": "\n\nBut the state’s overall rain deficit remains large, and the Sierra Nevada and the San Joaquin Valley are still experiencing major deficits, the U.S. Drought Monitor said Thursday.\n\nCalifornia is witnessing the all-conquering power behind nature, in a series of wet spells stretching back to a December snowstorm that ended a stubborn five-year drought in recent months.\n\nSnowfall totaled more than 40 inches in the Sierra Nevada, and the Sierra Fund recorded last week its first significant snowfall in five years in the eastern Sierra Nevada.\n\nCAPTION\n\nEllen DeGeneres issued an apology to her show's staff Monday morning in the wake of accusations of a toxic work environment, in which employees described enduring chronic bullying and harassment by show executives.\n\nEllen DeGeneres issued an apology to her show's staff Monday morning in the wake of accusations of a toxic work environment, in which employees described enduring chronic bullying and harassment by show",
